WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.250
Choose a steady position.

2
00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:06.590
You can sit, stand, or lie down, and you can adjust at any point.

3
00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:10.990
Keep your eyes open if that helps you feel oriented.

4
00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:18.800
Begin by noticing the room: a color, a shape, and one sound that confirms where you are.

5
00:00:31.454 --> 00:00:33.974
Now feel the ground or another surface beneath you.

6
00:00:35.674 --> 00:00:37.124
You do not have to imagine support.

7
00:00:38.824 --> 00:00:46.584
Look for direct evidence of it: pressure under the feet, the weight of the legs on a seat, the back meeting a chair, or the body resting on a bed.

8
00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:07.795
Choose the clearest point of contact.

9
00:01:09.495 --> 00:01:10.785
Stay with its shape.

10
00:01:12.485 --> 00:01:14.345
Is it broad or small?

11
00:01:16.045 --> 00:01:17.685
Even or changing?

12
00:01:19.385 --> 00:01:21.675
Warm, cool, firm, or soft?

13
00:01:23.375 --> 00:01:27.765
If none of these descriptions fit, simply know that contact is present.

14
00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:53.253
Let attention include a second point of support.

15
00:01:54.953 --> 00:01:57.793
Notice how the body's weight is distributed between the two.

16
00:01:59.493 --> 00:02:01.203
Nothing needs to be made symmetrical.

17
00:02:02.903 --> 00:02:06.113
The ground can receive you exactly as you are positioned now.

18
00:02:31.421 --> 00:02:35.241
See whether you can release one task to the surface beneath you.

19
00:02:36.941 --> 00:02:39.311
Perhaps the feet do not need to press so hard.

20
00:02:41.011 --> 00:02:44.081
Perhaps the shoulders can stop holding themselves quite so high.

21
00:02:45.781 --> 00:02:47.181
Do not force a change.

22
00:02:48.881 --> 00:02:50.861
Ask, and notice the answer.

23
00:03:13.639 --> 00:03:16.519
Feel breathing while you remain connected to the ground.

24
00:03:18.219 --> 00:03:21.439
On an inhale, the body may rise or widen a little.

25
00:03:23.139 --> 00:03:25.199
On an exhale, weight may settle.

26
00:03:26.899 --> 00:03:31.109
If no movement is clear, stay with pressure and contact instead.

27
00:03:56.417 --> 00:03:58.447
Thoughts may pull attention upward and away.

28
00:04:00.147 --> 00:04:03.827
When that happens, return through something physical.

29
00:04:05.527 --> 00:04:09.527
Feel the heel, the seat, the back, or a hand resting on the body.

30
00:04:11.227 --> 00:04:12.747
Let one contact point be enough.

31
00:04:38.055 --> 00:04:41.335
Now notice the edges of the body that are not touching a surface.

32
00:04:43.035 --> 00:04:46.505
Feel air at the face, around the arms, or across the hands.

33
00:04:48.205 --> 00:04:51.915
The body is both supported below and surrounded by space.

34
00:05:17.223 --> 00:05:24.483
For a few moments, hold the whole pattern lightly: ground below, body here, air around, breath moving.

35
00:05:26.183 --> 00:05:28.043
You do not need to focus perfectly.

36
00:05:29.743 --> 00:05:34.053
Let awareness move among these simple facts and return whenever it wanders.

37
00:06:05.689 --> 00:06:08.629
Check whether any area is asking for a small adjustment.

38
00:06:10.329 --> 00:06:12.109
Move slowly if you choose to move.

39
00:06:13.809 --> 00:06:19.119
Notice how support changes as the body changes position, and how the new position is received.

40
00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:39.640
Let your gaze become clearer.

41
00:06:41.340 --> 00:06:46.980
Take in the room again and listen for the nearest sound, then the farthest sound you can hear.

42
00:06:48.680 --> 00:06:52.250
Keep one point of contact in awareness as you prepare to continue.

43
00:06:54.650 --> 00:06:56.690
The ground does not remove what comes next.

44
00:06:58.390 --> 00:07:00.000
It gives you a place from which to meet it.
